import{_ as t,o,c as a,ag as i}from"./chunks/framework.CrXGS008.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Stations","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"repair-station/stations.md","filePath":"repair-station/stations.md"}'),s={name:"repair-station/stations.md"};function n(r,e,l,h,c,d){return o(),a("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[i('<h1 id="stations" tabindex="-1">Stations <a class="header-anchor" href="#stations" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Stations&quot;">​</a></h1><p>A station is a stopping area for vehicles, with a radius, a price percentage and, if you want one, a prop such as a tool chest placed next to it. Three stations come ready to use: <strong>Hayes Autos</strong>, <strong>Sandy Shores</strong> and <strong>Paleto Bay</strong>.</p><h2 id="how-a-repair-goes" tabindex="-1">How a repair goes <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-a-repair-goes" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How a repair goes&quot;">​</a></h2><ol><li>The driver stops inside the station radius. A prompt shows the lowest price.</li><li><strong>E</strong> opens the repair menu with the damage of the vehicle and the services, with their prices (job discounts and the station percentage included).</li><li>The price is paid, the engine is switched off and the bonnet opens. A progress bar runs for the duration of the service, with sound and sparks. Press <strong>X</strong> to cancel.</li><li>When it ends, the repaired parts are fixed and the vehicle can leave.</li></ol><p>The station refuses the repair when:</p><ul><li>the station is closed, or <code>Enabled</code> is off;</li><li>the player is not driving the vehicle, or the vehicle is not in the station area;</li><li>the vehicle is moving;</li><li>the station is already in use (one vehicle at a time);</li><li>the vehicle class is blocked (<code>BlockedClasses</code>);</li><li>the service repairs nothing on this vehicle and <code>RequireDamage</code> is on;</li><li>the player must wait for the cooldown (<code>CooldownSeconds</code>);</li><li>mechanics are on duty, see below;</li><li>the player cannot pay.</li></ul><p>If the player leaves the vehicle, drives away or cancels, or if the station is closed or deleted during the repair, the repair stops and the player is refunded the amount charged, on the account that was charged.</p><h2 id="mechanics-on-duty" tabindex="-1">Mechanics on duty <a class="header-anchor" href="#mechanics-on-duty" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Mechanics on duty&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Players who run a mechanic business should not lose customers to a free station. List their jobs in <code>MechanicJobs</code> and set <code>MaxMechanicsOnDuty</code>: while that many mechanics or more are on duty, every station is closed and tells players to call them. With <code>0</code>, stations never close for this reason.</p><h2 id="the-station-editor" tabindex="-1">The station editor <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-station-editor" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The station editor&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Open it with <code>/nay:repair</code>, or with <strong>Manage stations</strong> on the Repair Station page of <code>/nay</code>. It needs the scope <code>nay_repair.config</code>.</p><ol><li><strong>New station here</strong>: stand where vehicles should stop, in your vehicle or on foot. The station takes your position and heading.</li><li>Pick the vehicle position or the prop position and move it: <ul><li>arrows: forward, back, left, right, relative to the camera;</li><li>Page Up / Page Down: height;</li><li>Q / E: rotate;</li><li>Shift: fine steps.</li></ul></li><li><strong>To my position</strong> and <strong>To ground</strong> snap the selected element.</li><li>Set the name, radius, price percentage, blip and prop. Suggested props: <code>prop_toolchest_05</code>, <code>prop_toolchest_01</code>, <code>prop_carcreeper</code>, <code>prop_compressor_03</code>, or any model name.</li><li><strong>Enter</strong> saves, <strong>Backspace</strong> cancels. The station is live for every player right away.</li></ol><p>The manager also goes to a station, opens or closes it, and deletes it (press twice to confirm). The editor fills the <code>Stations</code> setting, described on the <a href="/repair-station/settings#stations">Settings</a> page. Each station gets an identifier that never changes.</p>',13)])])}const u=t(s,[["render",n]]);export{g as __pageData,u as default};
